    {
      "id": "expression-callbacks-and-hooks/conditional-disabled-target",
      "doc_id": "expression-callbacks-and-hooks",
      "claim": "The modern expressions map supports a props.disabled expression.",
      "conditions_json": "[]",
      "limits_json": "[]",
      "context": "Conditional disabled state using a field expression.",
      "source_quote": "| API | Relevant contract |\n| --- | --- |\n| `expressions: { 'props.disabled': fn }` | Public callback receives the field; read `field.model` and `field.options.formState` |\n| Legacy `expressionProperties` / `hideExpression` function | Model, formState, optional field arguments |\n| String expression | Evaluated with model, formState, field bindings |\n| Observable expression | Value stream applied to the targeted field property |\n\nEvidence: declarations [K01](sources.md#k01), evaluator [K07](sources.md#k07), tests [K25](sources.md#k25). One upstream test title still mentions the older arguments, but its assertion checks a field argument. Prefer declarations and assertions over the test title. An extra internal evaluation flag is not a reason to build application callbacks around undocumented arguments.",
      "source_start_offset": 125,
      "source_end_offset": 936,
      "status": "authored"
    },
    {
      "id": "expression-callbacks-and-hooks/conditional-hide-target",
      "doc_id": "expression-callbacks-and-hooks",
      "claim": "The modern expressions map supports a hide expression.",
      "conditions_json": "[]",
      "limits_json": "[]",
      "context": "Conditional visibility using a field expression.",
      "source_quote": "// Explanatory v6 fragment; assumes this leaf shares the relevant model scope.\nexpressions: {\n  'props.disabled': field => !field.model?.country,\n  hide: field => field.options?.formState?.mode === 'summary',\n}\n```\n\nDo not copy a legacy `(model) => model.country` callback into `expressions` without adapting it. For constant visibility use `hide: true/false` on the field; for conditional visibility use a supported expression. The pinned `FieldExpression` type is string/function/Observable, and the evaluator does not establish arbitrary boolean entries as a general expression API [K01](sources.md#k01), [K07](sources.md#k07).",
      "source_start_offset": 944,
      "source_end_offset": 1574,
      "status": "authored"
    },
    {
